{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 32, :comments ["<b>And you shall keep, to do, etc.</b> The explanation is that since the commandments He comes to command them depend on the Land, therefore He said to them that they should keep them — in the sense of (Genesis 37:11) ״וְאָבִיו שָׁמַר אֶת הַדָּבָר״ — and the intent is that they should be waiting to perform them. And the intent in this is that even though at the time He is speaking with them they are not able to perform them, they should be guarding the things to do them when the time arrives. And he concluded saying, <b>these are the statutes</b>, etc. — meaning, these are what I command you to keep and to do in the Land — because they depend on entering the Land, for there HaShem commanded to destroy all the [pagan worship] sites, and as long as they have not arrived there they are not able to perform them."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:16:43.942280240Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}